request:
the id of a lease that was granted a moment ago

POST /v3/lease/keepalive
{
  "ID": "4343"
}

response:
one chunked line: `{"result": {header, ID, TTL}}`, and the TTL is full again

HTTP 200 OK
{
  "result": {
    "ID": "4343",
    "TTL": "30",
    "header": {
      "cluster_id": "16080428633167090200",
      "member_id": "5200481858496138789",
      "raft_term": "2",
      "revision": "1"
    }
  }
}

request:
an id that was never granted — or was, and has since expired

POST /v3/lease/keepalive
{
  "ID": "999999"
}

response:
the same shape, carrying the id and no TTL at all

HTTP 200 OK
{
  "result": {
    "ID": "999999",
    "header": {
      "cluster_id": "1040952130671434959",
      "member_id": "6089127669819784103",
      "raft_term": "2",
      "revision": "1"
    }
  }
}
